# Depth of Field on D3D11 (0) or the render graph (1): Whiterun at 13:00 in clear weather, then Dragonsreach, a shot of each.
# Sub-effects this test expects enabled (under "PostProcessing" in SettingsUser.json): "Depth of Field" only, with its
# defaults (Auto Focus at the screen centre, Adaptive Gather, Performance rings), and for a second pair of runs
# "PostBlurSmoothing": 0.5 and "BokehMode": 1 (a custom aperture) to cover the post smoothing and shape passes.
# Every other sub-effect off: "Local Exposure", "Histogram Auto Exposure", "COD Bloom", "Lens Flare", "Motion Blur",
# "Physical Glare", "Camera", "Vignette", "Color Grading and Tone Mapping", "LUT", "Border": { "enabled": false }
# (or on, for those already ported). Cinematic Camera off; Effects11 must not own the tonemap.
# Look for "[ORG] Post Processing: chain built (input, dof, output; 19 passes" (16 DoF dispatches + input + 2 outputs with
# the defaults) and "the chain runs on the render graph". The two runs' shots should match: near/far blur and focus.
CS_ORG_POST_PROCESSING=1
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=600:set timescale to 0;601:set gamehour to 13;602:fw 81a;700:coc Whiterun;2000:fw 81a;2400:dclf:shot=whiterun;2500:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;3600:dclf:shot=dragonsreach
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=3700
CS_PP_ONLY=Depth of Field
